<title>INDIA: India's IDBI cuts prime rate to 14.5 pct.</title>
<headline>India's IDBI cuts prime rate to 14.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Industrial Development Bank of India (IDBI) on Monday said it will reduce its prime lending rate to 14.5 percent per annum from 15.0 percent effective July 1.</p>
<p>The new rate will be exclusive of taxes, a bank official said.  </p>
<p>&quot;The rate of interest on a particular loan will continue to be fixed within an interest band of 3.5 percentage points, depending upon the risk perception,&quot; an IDBI statement said.</p>
<p>IDBI is India's leading term-lending bank.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
